      "message": "refactor(log): library and UI diagnostics become tracing events\n\nThe last slice of #163. The remaining eprintln! refusals and fallbacks in\ncamcraft-cl, -geometry, -motion, -sim and -tools are tracing events (warn;\nthe opt-in projection profile at info), and each standalone bin installs a\nstderr subscriber with the app's CAMCRAFT_LOG / RUST_LOG rule so they still\nreach its terminal. The ui diag seam emits tracing events natively, and the\nnative window, GPU bring-up, quit hook, frame watch and headless proof\nspeak through it; only test-only code still prints directly.\n\ntracing and tracing-subscriber were already workspace dependencies; no new\ncrate and no camcraft-* edge.\n\nPinned by cl refusal_log::a_refused_axis_or_angle_is_a_warning_under_the_cl_target\nand ui diag::tests::diag_lines_are_tracing_events_at_their_level.\n\nFixes #163\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
